course: dictionary
lesson: 12473
title: Deformed: a changed shape
level: primary-5
stars: 3
explain: Deformed means that something has had its usual shape changed or twisted, so it is no longer the proper shape. Look at the clues: «The spring was deformed after the heavy box fell on it.» A spring should be neatly coiled, so a squashed spring has lost its proper shape.
explain: Deformed can also be a verb. To deform something is to change its shape by force or heat. «The heat began to deform the plastic ruler.» The clue is heat, which can soften things and change their shape. Try your meaning in the sentence: "The heat began to change the shape of the plastic ruler" still makes sense, so you have it.
explain: Be kind when you talk about people. Today people say «a different shape» or «a limb difference», because the word deformed can hurt. Choose words that show respect.
fact: «Deformed» means having a shape that has been changed or twisted, so it is not the usual or proper shape.
fact: To deform something means to change its shape by force or heat.
fact: The forms of the verb are deform, deforms, deformed and deforming.
fact: «The metal bar was deformed when the crane lifted too much weight.» The force from the crane bent it out of shape.
fact: In stories, monsters are sometimes called deformed, but this word should never be used to mock real people.
exercise: «The spring was deformed by the heavy box.» What does deformed mean here? | *Changed in shape by force | Made of wood | Very shiny and new | Lost in the room
exercise: What does the verb deform mean? | *To change its shape by force or heat | To count the parts | To cool something down quickly | To make something bright
exercise: Find the verb in «The heat began to deform the plastic ruler.» | plastic | heat | ruler | *deform
test: What does deformed mean in «The tin can was deformed when we stood on it»? | Very cold | Shiny and clean | Full of water | *Squashed out of its proper shape
test: Which is the kind way to talk about a person whose body is a different shape? | *A different shape | Deformed | Monster | Strange-looking
exam: Which sentence uses deformed correctly? | The pencil was deformed, so it was very sharp. | I deformed my lunch by eating it quickly. | *The bent spring was deformed when a heavy box fell on it.
